# Local, untracked files a new git worktree needs to run, copied from the main checkout by the
# worktrees plugin (its worktree-hydrate.sh, run by its EnterWorktree hook and the starter's
# post-checkout githook). One rule per line:
#   required <path>   a file the worktree cannot run without (missing ones are reported)
#   optional <path>   copied when present
# A path is a literal file or a folder ending in /** (copied whole). Paths must stay inside the
# repo. Heavy dependency folders (node_modules, a Python .venv) do not belong here: install
# them in the worktree instead.
optional .env
optional .env.local
